feat(close): the one-shot close binds the Continuity Result itself when it needs agent authority only

A Continuity feature without a bound Result stopped the one-shot close with a
five-step repair list although every step is agent authority; the first
Antigravity greenfield run paid a detour for it. The close now runs the
bootstrap plan, its apply action (owner route or direct), the agent-run
reconcile and commit-pipeline-owned --agent itself, then enters the close once
more so State, addenda, acknowledgement, acceptance question, Verify and the
close request are all derived at the HEAD the bootstrap commit produced.

A plan or completion that needs the PO signature still stops, naming the
printed signature command and what was written; a second bootstrap is a typed
stop (ONESHOT-RESULT-BOOTSTRAP-LOOP); later stops say what the bootstrap
committed. An acceptance answer given before the new HEAD existed is not
carried over it, and a decline with an unbound Result still stops unchanged.

